to open up with each other.

00:01:51.196 --> 00:01:54.289
We've only seen each
other around the office

00:01:54.289 --> 00:01:56.589
and a little downtime afterwards,
so this will be really

00:01:56.589 --> 00:01:58.499
good to dig in there.

00:01:58.499 --> 00:02:02.878
So where do you guys see
yourself in like five years?

00:02:02.878 --> 00:02:04.389
- I don't like thinking about that.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:06.212
I don't even know where
I'm gonna be next year.

00:02:06.212 --> 00:02:08.774
- I would like to think
that I would be working at

00:02:08.774 --> 00:02:11.471
least someplace where I'm telling stories.

00:02:11.471 --> 00:02:13.499
I mean, that's why I moved out here, so.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.726
My endgame really is to
just make enough money

00:02:15.726 --> 00:02:18.242
to support myself and my
family, doing what I love to do.

00:02:18.242 --> 00:02:20.215
- Are you planning on being
married in five years?

00:02:20.215 --> 00:02:22.577
- I don't know if I'll be
married in five years but--

00:02:22.577 --> 00:02:25.071
- When do you think you wanna get married?

00:02:25.071 --> 00:02:27.338
- Really late twenties to early thirties.

00:02:27.338 --> 00:02:28.708
- I don't know, I see myself later.

00:02:28.708 --> 00:02:30.263
Like mid to late thirties.

00:02:30.263 --> 00:02:32.772
- I feel like I would be
okay with getting married

00:02:32.772 --> 00:02:36.230
like late twenties but
then waiting to have kids

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:37.673
so that I could travel.

00:02:37.673 --> 00:02:39.983
- There's a lot of things
that we unfortunately have

00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:41.463
to let go as we get older,

00:02:41.463 --> 00:02:43.699
so as an adult, to be
able to just pick a night

00:02:43.699 --> 00:02:46.047
of the week and just put on a onesie,

00:02:46.047 --> 00:02:47.691
as silly as that all sounds,

00:02:47.691 --> 00:02:49.217
it's incredibly gratifying.

00:02:49.217 --> 00:02:50.259
- Should we do this again?

00:02:50.259 --> 00:02:52.390
- I'd be down for that. Also
if it's a larger slumber party,

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:53.714
maybe like seven to ten people.

00:02:53.714 --> 00:02:55.699
- That many people could
build a dope ass fort.

00:02:55.699 --> 00:02:58.679
- Oh man, we should've built a fort.

